'''DesprésDesprés''' ({{lang|ca|Després Després}}, "after after") is a restaurant in [[Sant Cristòfor]], [[Balboa]], serving a family-style tasting menu that combines haute Zong culinary minimalism with the maximalist flavors of Black Balboan cooking. The restaurant was established in 2016 by mother [[Adelaida Paredes]] and daughter [[Yolanda Paredes]], and has been recognised at Nº4 on [[Abyala's 50 Best Restaurants]] (2020) and Nº50 on [[The World's 50 Best Restaurants]] (2024). It is known for its group-only dining policy: reservations are accepted exclusively for parties of four or more, with a "mix" option available for smaller groups who wish to share a table.

== Name ==

The name is a doubling of the Catalan word {{lang|ca|després}} ("after"), yielding {{lang|ca|després després}} — "after after." The name was chosen by Adelaida and Yolanda Paredes to reflect the restaurant's philosophy of what comes after the expected: after the first course, after the first impression, after the tradition. It also carries a personal resonance: the restaurant is the life that came after Adelaida's decades of cafeteria work, and after Yolanda's culinary training abroad.

== History ==

=== Adelaida Paredes ===

[[Adelaida Paredes]] (born c. 1960) spent over thirty years as a line cook in the institutional cafeterias of [[Sant Bart]], preparing daily meals for government workers, hospital staff, and schoolchildren. She was known among her colleagues for the quality of her personal cooking — the dishes she brought from home, rooted in the Black Balboan traditions of the Jala lowlands, were sought after by every kitchen crew she worked with — but she never cooked professionally outside the cafeteria system. The recipes she developed over three decades of institutional cooking, adapted to limited budgets and bulk preparation, formed the foundation of what would become the DesprésDesprés menu.

=== Yolanda Paredes ===

[[Yolanda Paredes]] (born c. 1988) grew up in her mother's kitchen in Sant Bart, absorbing the Black Balboan repertoire before leaving for Volisania at eighteen to enroll at the [[Institut Culinari de Volisania]], the premier culinary institute in the world. She trained in classical technique and staged at several Volisanian restaurants before returning to Balboa in her mid-twenties. Her culinary education exposed her to the Zong culinary tradition that had become central to Sant Cristòfor's fine dining scene, and she began to imagine a restaurant that would place her mother's cooking — the food of Black Balboan working-class kitchens — on the same table as the refined Zong techniques she had learned abroad.

=== Founding (2016) ===

The two women opened DesprésDesprés in 2016 at 843 [[Plaça Marcos Aldana]], a residential square in a historically Black Balboan neighbourhood of Sant Cristòfor. The space was modest — a single dining room with communal tables, no linens, and an open kitchen — and the concept was immediate: every dish would be served family-style, and every reservation would require a group. The restaurant announced from its opening that it would not seat solo diners or pairs at their own tables; the meal was designed to be shared, and the table was the unit of service.

[[File:DesprésDesprés dining room.png|thumb|The communal dining room, 2019]]

=== Critical reception ===

DesprésDesprés received immediate attention for its group-only policy, which was discussed in local and international press as both a provocation and a statement of culinary philosophy. The food, however, drew the more sustained acclaim. Critics identified the restaurant's central achievement as the synthesis of two traditions that had previously occupied separate worlds in Balboa: the spare, precise, ingredient-driven minimalism of haute Zong cooking and the bold, layered, unapologetic maximalism of Black Balboan home cooking. In 2020, DesprésDesprés was named Nº4 on [[Abyala's 50 Best Restaurants]], and in 2024 it entered [[The World's 50 Best Restaurants]] at Nº50.

== Cuisine ==

DesprésDesprés serves a single family-style tasting menu each evening. The menu changes seasonally, but the underlying philosophy is consistent: Zong technique applied to Black Balboan ingredients and flavor profiles, served in portions designed to be passed and shared rather than plated individually.

The cuisine is described by Yolanda Paredes as "Zong restraint, Balboan abundance." The Zong tradition contributes precision of execution, respect for the integrity of individual ingredients, and a disciplined approach to seasoning — each element on the plate is intended to be tasted distinctly. The Black Balboan tradition contributes the opposite impulse: layered seasoning, multiple textures in a single dish, generous portions, and the principle that a meal should overwhelm before it satisfies.

[[File:DesprésDesprés spread.png|thumb|A family-style spread at DesprésDesprés]]

=== Signature approach ===

A representative course might present a whole braised chicken — the primary protein of Black Balboan cooking, treated here with the precision of a Zong broth reduction — alongside a set of side dishes that each carry a distinct seasoning register: a chili-oil slaw, a cassava mash with fermented bean paste, a plate of greens dressed in citrus and numbing pepper, and a bowl of rice seasoned with coconut and soy. The diner is expected to combine these elements at will, constructing each bite from the communal table. The effect is deliberately overwhelming: where a Zong tasting menu would isolate each flavor for contemplation, DesprésDesprés invites the diner to pile, mix, and discover.

=== Non-alcoholic pairing ===

DesprésDesprés offers a non-alcoholic pairing with every reservation. The pairing consists of a sequence of house-made drinks — herbal infusions, fruit shrubs, spiced teas, and fermented beverages — designed to complement the progression of courses. The decision to offer a non-alcoholic pairing rather than a wine or sake program was deliberate: Adelaida Paredes, who does not drink alcohol, insisted that the beverage program reflect the same accessibility and communal spirit as the food. The pairing is included in the cost of the meal.

== Group-only policy ==

DesprésDesprés accepts reservations only for parties of four or more. The policy is rooted in the restaurant's culinary philosophy: the family-style menu is designed to be shared, and the portions, pacing, and presentation assume a communal table. Solo diners and pairs cannot experience the menu as intended, and the restaurant has declined to offer individual plating.

=== "Mix" reservation ===

For parties of fewer than four, the restaurant offers a "mix" reservation ({{lang|ca|reserva mixta}}), in which smaller groups or individuals are seated together at a communal table and share the same family-style meal. The cost is the same as a standard reservation. The mix table has become one of the restaurant's most distinctive features, and is frequently cited by critics as the most memorable way to experience the meal: strangers sharing food from the same plates, in a restaurant explicitly designed around the principle that eating is a collective act.

